{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Oh it's all your fault if I ain’t sleepin'
[C7]live on dreams instead of eatin'
[F7]I'm just a wreck and [Bb7]it's all your [Eb]fault
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
And [Eb]it's all your fault if I ain’t playin'
[C7]Havin' fun and if I'm stayin'
[F7]All by myself [Bb7]it's all your [Eb]fault
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G7]When you said that we were through
I [Ab]tried to find somebody new
But [F7]I found out it wouldn't do
[Bb7]Cause I'd rather be alone than with somebody new
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
And [Eb]it's all your fault when I'm a Grandpa
If [C7]my grandkids don't call you Grandma
[F7]I'll just tell 'em [Bb7]it's all your [Eb]fault
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F7]I'll just tell 'em [Bb7]it's all your [Eb]fault
